{{Bagua|qq=}} '''Kun''' (坤) is one of the {{ill|Bagua|ja|八卦|qq=}}. Its trigram form is {{resize|125%|'''☷'''|qq=}} and consists of three Yin (⚋) {{ill|Yao (lines)|ja|爻|qq=}}. It is also one of the {{ill|Sixty-Four Hexagrams|ja|六十四卦|qq=}}, known as {{ill|Kun as Earth|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun為地|qq=}}, consisting of Kun below and Kun above.
== Trigram Symbolism == Kun symbolizes earth, compliance, cattle, the abdomen, the mother, grandmother, feminine virtues, the stomach, the right shoulder, support roles, sluggishness, the masses, and hesitation. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=}}, it represents {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|qq=}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|qq=}} system, Kun is associated with {{ill|Yi (Heavenly Stem)|ja|乙|1=Kinoto (乙)|qq=}}, the Wood element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=}}, and the {{ill|east|ja|東|qq=}} among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|qq=}}. Alternatively, it can also correspond to {{ill|Gui (Heavenly Stem)|ja|癸|1=Mizunoto (癸)|qq=}}, the Water element, and the {{ill|north|ja|北|qq=}}.
== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=}}, Kun corresponds to the {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|qq=}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|qq=}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|Kan=c|lt=Kan (☵)|qq=}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt\=Gen (☶)|lt=Gen (☶)|qq=}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|qq=}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|qq=}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|qq=}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|2=ja|3=兌|4=zh-yue|5=兌卦|6=ko|7=태 (괘)|8=fr|9=Duì|10=nl|11=Meer (trigram)|12=pt|13=Duì (I Ching)|14=zh-min-nan|15=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt=Dui (☱)|qq=}}, and {{ill|Qian|ja|乾|1=Qian (Bagua)|lt=Qian|lt=Qian (☰)|qq=}}—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Kun corresponds to the area between {{ill|Wei (Earthly Branch)|ja|未|qq=}} and {{ill|Shen (Earthly Branch)|ja|申|qq=}}, known as *Hitsujisaru* (ひつじさる).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=}}, Kun is the eighth in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing {{ill|north|ja|北|qq=}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the extreme of Yin.
