[[sn:Kun (Bagua)]] [[ja:坤]] [[ja:震]] [[ja:巽]] [[ja:太極]] [[ja:乾]] [[ja:兌]] [[ja:艮]] [[ja:離]] [[ja:九星]] [[ja:魔方陣]] [[ja:後天定位盤]] [[ja:五行思想]] [[ja:木]] [[ja:火]] [[ja:土]] [[ja:金]] [[ja:水]] [[ja:十干]] [[ja:十二支]] [[ja:八卦]] [[ja:易経]] [[ja:禹]] [[ja:夏王朝]] [[ja:洛水]] [[ja:洛書]] [[ja:河図洛書]] [[ja:陰陽道]] [[ja:方位]] [[ja:運勢]] [[ja:吉凶]] [[ja:一白水星]] [[ja:北]] [[ja:坎]] [[ja:二黒土星]] [[ja:三碧木星]] [[ja:東]] [[ja:四緑木星]] [[ja:五黄土星]] [[ja:六白金星]] [[ja:七赤金星]] [[ja:西]] [[ja:八白土星]] [[ja:九紫火星]] [[ja:南]] [[ja:太陽系]] [[ja:相性]] [[ja:吉方位]] [[ja:易]] [[ja:高島易断]] [[ja:風水]] [[ja:気学]] [[ja:陰陽五行説]] [[ja:暦注]] [[en:draft:Kun (Bagua)]] [[sn:Kun]] [[fr:K%C5%ABn (symbole asiatique)]] [[en:Kun]] [[ar:Kun (Bagua)]]

{{Bagua|qq=}} '''Kun''' (坤) is one of the {{ill|Bagua|ja|八卦|qq=|qq=draft}}. Its trigram form is {{resize|125%|'''☷'''|qq=}} and consists of three Yin (⚋) {{ill|Yao (lines)|ja|爻|qq=|qq=draft}}. It is also one of the {{ill|Sixty-Four Hexagrams|ja|六十四卦|qq=|qq=draft}}, known as {{ill|Kun as Earth|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun為地|qq=|qq=draft}}, consisting of Kun below and Kun above.
== Trigram Symbolism == Kun symbolizes earth, compliance, cattle, the abdomen, the mother, grandmother, feminine virtues, the stomach, the right shoulder, support roles, sluggishness, the masses, and hesitation. As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=|qq=draft}}, it represents {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|qq=|qq=draft}}.
In the {{ill|Na Jia|ja|納甲|qq=|qq=draft}} system, Kun is associated with {{ill|Yi (Heavenly Stem)|ja|乙|1=Kinoto (乙)|qq=|qq=draft}}, the Wood element in {{ill|Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|lt=Wuxing|ja|五行思想|1=Wuxing (Chinese philosophy)|2=ja|3=五行思想|lt=Five Elements (Wuxing)|qq=|qq=draft}}, and the {{ill|east|ja|東|qq=|qq=draft}} among the {{ill|Five Directions|ja|五方|qq=|qq=draft}}. Alternatively, it can also correspond to {{ill|Gui (Heavenly Stem)|ja|癸|1=Mizunoto (癸)|qq=|qq=draft}}, the Water element, and the {{ill|north|ja|北|qq=|qq=draft}}.
== Direction == As a {{ill|cardinal direction|ja|方位|qq=|qq=draft}}, Kun corresponds to the {{ill|southwest|ja|西南|qq=|qq=draft}}. When the four cardinal directions (east, west, south, north) are divided into twelve parts using the {{ill|Earthly Branches|ja|十二支|qq=|qq=draft}}, intermediate directions such as northeast, southeast, southwest, and northwest cannot be fully expressed. To address this, the eight trigrams—{{ill|Kan|ja|坎|1=Kan (Bagua)|lt=Kan|Kan=c|lt=Kan (☵)|qq=|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Gen|ja|艮|1=Gen (Bagua)|lt=Gen|lt\=Gen (☶)|lt=Gen (☶)|qq=|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Zhen|ja|震|1=Zhen (Bagua)|lt=Zhen|lt=Zhen (☳)|qq=|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Xun|ja|巽|1=Xun (Bagua)|lt=Xun|lt=Xun (☴)|qq=|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Li|ja|離|1=Li (Bagua)|lt=Li|lt=Li (☲)|qq=|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Kun|ja|坤|1=Kun (Bagua)|lt=Kun|lt=Kun (☷)|qq=|qq=draft}}, {{ill|Dui|ja|兌|1=Dui (Bagua)|2=ja|3=兌|4=zh-yue|5=兌卦|6=ko|7=태 (괘)|8=fr|9=Duì|10=nl|11=Meer (trigram)|12=pt|13=Duì (I Ching)|14=zh-min-nan|15=Tōe-kòa|lt=Dui (兌)|1=Dui (Bagua)|lt=Dui|lt=Dui (☱)|qq=|qq=draft}}, and {{ill|Qian|ja|乾|1=Qian (Bagua)|lt=Qian|lt=Qian (☰)|qq=|qq=draft}}—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Kun corresponds to the area between {{ill|Wei (Earthly Branch)|ja|未|qq=|qq=draft}} and {{ill|Shen (Earthly Branch)|ja|申|qq=|qq=draft}}, known as *Hitsujisaru* (ひつじさる).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=|qq=draft}}, Kun is the eighth in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing {{ill|north|ja|北|qq=|qq=draft}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the extreme of Yin.
