le/Qian (Bagua)|qq=}}—are used to indicate directions<ref>「[https://www.ndl.go.jp/koyomi/chapter3/s2.html 干支2方位神]」National Diet Library, accessed December 16, 2021.</ref>. Kun corresponds to the area between {{ill|Wei (Earthly Branch)|ja|未|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Wei (Earthly Branch)|qq=}} and {{ill|Shen (Earthly Branch)|ja|申|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shen (Earthly Branch)|qq=}}, known as *Hitsujisaru* (ひつじさる).
== Earlier Heaven Arrangement == In the {{ill|Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|ja|伏羲先天八卦|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Fuxi Earlier Heaven Bagua|qq=}}, Kun is the eighth in sequence and is positioned as one of the four cardinal trigrams, representing {{ill|north|ja|北|qq=|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/north|qq=}}. In terms of Yin-Yang transformation, it represents the extreme of Yin.
